<resources>

    <!--
        French.

        Terminology held to throughout:
        · «jetons» are the physical tokens, «espèces» the real money. Keeping those apart is the
          app’s central hazard and matters as much here as in English.
        · «banque» is the bank that issues and buys back chips; the pot stays «pot».
        · «petite blinde», «grosse blinde», «cave» (buy-in), «recave» (rebuy) and «tapis» are the
          terms French-speaking players actually use.
        · Field names arrive as arguments inside error messages, so those messages are phrased
          with a colon («Petite blinde : champ obligatoire») rather than agreeing with the noun’s
          gender, which the app cannot know.
        · Apostrophes are typographic (’), which needs no escaping and is correct French.
    -->

